.TH BUFFER_STUBBORN 3
.SH NAME
buffer_stubborn \- robustly perform a buffered I/O operation
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <buffer.h>
.P
int \fBbuffer_stubborn\fP(\fIop\fP, \fIfd\fP, \fIx\fP, \fIn\fP, \fIb\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbuffer_stubborn\fP attempts to perform an I/O operation \fIop\fP on file descriptor \fIfd\fP, ensuring the full amount \fIn\fP bytes is processed from/to buffer \fIx\fP.
.P
It repeatedly calls the operation \fIop\fP until either all \fIn\fP bytes are successfully handled or an error occurs. If the operation is interrupted by a signal (\fBEINTR\fP), the call continues automatically.
.P
The \fIb\fP argument is passed through to the \fIop\fP function. The \fIop\fP function must match the \fBbuffer_op_proto\fP signature:
.RS
.B typedef ssize_t buffer_op_proto(fd_type, void*, size_t, struct buffer*);
.RE
.P
The \fIop\fP function should return the number of bytes processed, 0 for EOF, or -1 on error.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 upon success (all \fIn\fP bytes processed), or -1 on error. If -1 is returned, \fIerrno\fP is set to indicate the cause of the failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
buffer(3)